{"text":"A poem by the people, the poor, the protestants, the muslim, the jew, the native, the immigrant, the black, the brown, the blind, the brave, the undocumented and undeterred, the woman, the man, the non-binary, the white, the trans, the ally, to all of the above and more. Tyrants fear the poet. Now that we know it, we can't blow it, we owe it to show it, not slow it, although it hurts to sow it. When the world starts to blow at hope, we must bestow it like a wick in the poet so it can grow lit, bringing with it new stories to rewrite. The story of a Puerto Rico depleted, but not defeated, a history written that need not be repeated, a nation composed.","words":[{"text":"A","start":0.0,"end":0.42},{"text":"poem","start":0.42,"end":0.64},{"text":"by","start":0.64,"end":1.06},{"text":"the","start":1.06,"end":1.24},{"text":"people","start":1.24,"end":1.6,"punct":","},{"text":"the","start":1.76,"end":1.82},{"text":"poor","start":1.82,"end":2.22,"punct":","},{"text":"the","start":2.64,"end":2.7},{"text":"protestants","start":2.7,"end":3.38,"punct":","},{"text":"the","start":3.54,"end":3.62},{"text":"muslim","start":3.62,"end":4.18,"punct":","},{"text":"the","start":4.36,"end":4.5},{"text":"jew","start":4.5,"end":4.76,"punct":","},{"text":"the","start":4.98,"end":5.1},{"text":"native","start":5.1,"end":5.46,"punct":","},{"text":"the","start":5.7,"end":5.74},{"text":"immigrant","start":5.74,"end":6.14,"punct":","},{"text":"the","start":6.32,"end":6.38},{"text":"black","start":6.38,"end":6.68,"punct":","},{"text":"the","start":6.86,"end":6.88},{"text":"brown","start":6.88,"end":7.16,"punct":","},{"text":"the","start":7.32,"end":7.36},{"text":"blind","start":7.36,"end":7.66,"punct":","},{"text":"the","start":7.78,"end":7.86},{"text":"brave","start":7.86,"end":8.3,"punct":","},{"text":"the","start":8.44,"end":8.74},{"text":"undocumented","start":8.74,"end":9.54},{"text":"and","start":9.54,"end":9.92},{"text":"undeterred","start":9.92,"end":10.76,"punct":","},{"text":"t